  "corrections_after_the_fact": [
    "Run-level verdicts above exclude an operator artifact: the source skill was edited while runs were in flight (references/evaluation.md during haiku, references/runtimes.md during fable), which scored both as 'a protected path changed'. The runtime is handed a copy and never sees the live skill. Fixed in bench.py: a run's verdict protects only the copy; a change to the source skill is a round-level finding (verdict PASS_WITH_SOURCE_DRIFT).",
    "The first fable attempt recorded cost_usd null. It had hit --max-budget-usd 0.75 (subtype error_max_budget_usd, terminal_reason budget_exhausted) and exited 1 with a non-result envelope the adapter did not parse. Real charge US$ 1.0525 for 76,760 context tokens and no answer. Fixed in runtimes.py: usage and cost are parsed before the exit code is judged, and a budget-capped run is NOT_RUN."
  ],
